# 低频词汇 List01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List01核心词汇

{{abolish}}{/əˈbɒlɪʃ/}{废除；取消}{The government abolished the outdated law.}}
{{abrupt}}{/əˈbrʌpt/}{突然的；唐突的}{The meeting came to an abrupt end.}}
{{absorb}}{/əbˈzɔːb/}{吸收；吸引}{Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere.}}
{{abuse}}{/əˈbjuːs/}{滥用；虐待}{The abuse of power is a serious issue in any society.}}
{{accommodate}}{/əˈkɒmədeɪt/}{容纳；适应}{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}
{{accomplish}}{/əˈkʌmplɪʃ/}{完成；实现}{She accomplished her goal of running a marathon.}}
{{accumulate}}{/əˈkjuːmjuleɪt/}{积累；堆积}{Dust accumulates quickly in unused rooms.}}
{{accustom}}{/əˈkʌstəm/}{使习惯}{It took time to accustom himself to the new environment.}}
{{admire}}{/ədˈmaɪər/}{钦佩；欣赏}{I admire her dedication to her work.}}
{{admission}}{/ədˈmɪʃn/}{准入；承认}{Admission to the program is highly competitive.}}
{{adventure}}{/ədˈventʃər/}{冒险；冒险经历}{Traveling to remote places is a great adventure.}}
{{advisable}}{/ədˈvaɪzəbl/}{明智的；可取的}{It is advisable to save money for emergencies.}}
{{afterward}}{/ˈɑːftəwəd/}{后来；以后}{We went to dinner and afterward saw a movie.}}
{{agony}}{/ˈæɡəni/}{极度痛苦}{The patient was in agony before the medication took effect.}}
{{aircraft}}{/ˈeəkrɑːft/}{飞机；航空器}{The aircraft landed safely despite the bad weather.}}
{{alarm}}{/əˈlɑːm/}{警报；惊恐}{The fire alarm went off in the middle of the night.}}
{{alcohol}}{/ˈælkəhɒl/}{酒精；酒}{Excessive consumption of alcohol damages the liver.}}
{{allege}}{/əˈledʒ/}{指控；宣称}{The suspect is alleged to have committed the crime.}}
{{alliance}}{/əˈlaɪəns/}{联盟；同盟}{The two countries formed a military alliance.}}
{{allocate}}{/ˈæləkeɪt/}{分配；拨出}{The government allocated funds for disaster relief.}}
{{alongside}}{/əˌlɒŋˈsaɪd/}{在...旁边}{She sat alongside her colleague during the meeting.}}
{{amaze}}{/əˈmeɪz/}{使惊奇；使惊叹}{The magician's tricks amazed the audience.}}
{{ambition}}{/æmˈbɪʃn/}{野心；抱负}{Her ambition is to become a world-renowned scientist.}}
{{amuse}}{/əˈmjuːz/}{逗乐；消遣}{The comedian amused the crowd with his jokes.}}
{{anchor}}{/ˈæŋkər/}{锚；主持人}{The news anchor delivered the evening bulletin.}}
{{anniversary}}{/ˌænɪˈvɜːsəri/}{周年纪念}{The company celebrated its 50th anniversary.}}
{{annoy}}{/əˈnɔɪ/}{使恼怒；打扰}{Loud music from neighbors can be very annoying.}}
{{anonymous}}{/əˈnɒnɪməs/}{匿名的；无名的}{The donation was made by an anonymous benefactor.}}
{{anticipate}}{/ænˈtɪsɪpeɪt/}{预期；期望}{We did not anticipate such a strong response.}}
{{anxiety}}{/æŋˈzaɪəti/}{焦虑；不安}{Exam anxiety is common among students.}}
